WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.650
- [Student] Something your
teachers don't want you

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.010
to know with online school.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:05.420
If you really don't
feel like typing notes,

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.590
just press your FN key twice.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:10.760
This will literally type
what your teacher is saying

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:12.517
and you won't have to write notes.

00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:15.184
(playful music)

00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:25.880
Instead of Google, use Google Scholar.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.500
Because once you do this,
you can literally press

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.600
these buttons and it
cites everything for you.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.420
And they have more precise articles.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:34.910
They're called email trackers.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.330
So I can tell when my
teachers have opened my emails

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.220
and how many times and if they haven't.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.760
So when they say this, you'll know.

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:42.593
You'll just know.

00:00:42.593 --> 00:00:44.920
Go to the Google app and
press the camera icon.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.650
They have a homework section underneath.

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:47.710
Scan your homework with this.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:50.060
And it'll literally tell
you the right answers.

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:52.390
It's called the YouTube Transcript.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:55.010
This basically shows you
everything that's being said

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:55.843
in the video.

00:00:55.843 --> 00:00:57.370
And you can press Control + F.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.900
if you're ever given a worksheet,

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.840
just press the keywords
that you're looking for

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:01.830
and they'll come up here

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:04.241
and you won't have to
watch the whole video.

00:01:04.241 --> 00:01:06.908
(playful music)

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.230
A lot of teachers upload
their lessons from Zoom

00:01:18.230 --> 00:01:21.410
to the cloud converter, and
it gives us audio transcript.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:26.090
Hypothetically, you could
copy-paste all of the transcripts,

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.230
put them into one document,

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:29.550
and then when you're
doing open-book exams,

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.020
you press Control + F and search keywords.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:34.490
So you'd practically get
every question right.

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.020
You don't have to read your article guide.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.200
Instead, use Podcastle
free Chrome extension.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.160
Convert your articles into podcasts.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.740
Make a shared document like a Google doc.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.170
That's a study guide
for midterm and finals.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:48.453
Now share this document
with everyone in your class.

00:01:48.453 --> 00:01:50.700
And get everyone to add stuff in.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:52.850
Now you can learn off
other people's things

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:54.350
and they can learn off yours.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:01:56.230
If you forget to hand in an assignment

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.460
and you're past the time,

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:00.070
go to your Time and Date
settings and change them.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.190
The portal will reset and
you actually won't be late.

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:06.170
Instead of Google, use Google Scholar.

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:08.750
This will help you find
more reliable sources

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.030
and it's easier to navigate,

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:11.840
especially for research projects.

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:13.450
If you don't know how
to start off your essay,

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.180
do it with a quote.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.480
And then also explain the quote.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:20.060
This adds more words to your essay

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.650
and it acts as a hook
to engage your reader.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.130
If you're allowed to pick
your own essay topic,

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.360
choose one that makes you angry.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.150
This will allow you to rant
on and on about your topic

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:31.980
and you won't be worried about being short

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.980
of the word limit.

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.850
Once you're done writing your essay,

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.600
copy and paste it onto
a word-to-text reader.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.280
This will read out your essay,

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.150
and will allow you to catch your mistakes.

00:02:41.150 --> 00:02:43.510
When you're doing research
on your essay topic,

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:46.350
put PPT after your research topic.

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:47.730
This will bring up PowerPoints

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.790
which have important
and concise information

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.960
about your research topic

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.660
that will help you
understand what to include

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:53.800
in your essay and what not to.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:55.470
Do you suck at math?

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.460
Well, here's a tool to help you with that.

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:58.880
It's called Mathchops.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.970
It's a math prep tool that has a database

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:04.040
of the most common SAT and ACT questions.

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:06.460
They use an algorithm to
check what you're bad at

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.340
and help you with that

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.370
in the form of games

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.413
which is so fun.

